WEBVTT

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.870
Long time, Fuuka-chan.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.540
Takeshita-sensei!

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.730
Huh, do you know each other?

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:26.430
She helped us out at Gama Gama.

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.200
Thanks for all the help 
when I went into labor.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.010
Are you back at work?

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:32.140
Yeah.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.530
I'm going to be working
 at Tingarla, too.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.640
Really?

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.350
She's here to say "hi" 
to the penguins team.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:41.350
Chiyu-san!

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.850
This is Takeshita-sensei.

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.950
I'm Takeshita.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.850
Nice to meet you.

00:00:47.510 --> 00:00:51.150
Takeshita-sensei will be working 
with us exclusively going forward.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.280
Looking forward to it!

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.280
Looking forward to it.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.600
Huh? Have I seen you somewhere?

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.100
Is something wrong?

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.110
No, it's nothing.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.520
Shall we have you take a look 
at the eggs, then?

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.950
Please and thank you.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.010
How many days has it been?

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.640
Today's day 35.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.930
We've confirmed that it's a sperm egg.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.030
They usually hatch in about 38 days 
after they've been laid.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:51.440
It should be any day now.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:53.940
We're staying overnight?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:54.840
Yeah.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.570
It's the first baby we've had 
since Tingarla opened, after all.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.990
We want to be ready to respond overnight, 
in case anything goes wrong.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.290
I'm in!

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.460
I'll do it.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:10.650
It sounds fun, like training camp!

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:12.360
You're pretty into it.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.040
Babies are popular, so there's hope 
that we can use it to draw guests.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.160
It'll be rough, but I'm counting
on you to work together.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.430
Okay...

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:25.550
Let me know if there's anything 
you're worried about.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:27.220
Boss, a minute?

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:31.740
I can't have my shift being
changed out of nowhere.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.600
Oh, of course.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:34.480
Can you not make it?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.000
Sorry, I can't stay overnight.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.310
All right.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.220
I'll put together a schedule without you.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.950
So cute!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.460
He's gotten so big!

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.740
He just turned ten months old.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.800
I'm so relieved we found a nursery 
he could go to this past spring.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:00.360
Relieved? How so?

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.510
I do want to be with my baby, 
but I wanted to work, too.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.300
He's still so young.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.510
Isn't it going to be rough?

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.240
Of course.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.650
He cries every time we
leave him at the nursery.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.520
I have to be a monster and sprint to work.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:18.020
That sounds difficult.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:20.940
I love my work, though, so I tough it out.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:26.060
All the creatures at the aquarium 
give me strength.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:27.950
I know what you mean!

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:30.840
Okay, I'm going to get going.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:34.560
I've been doing three-day weeks for a while, 
so I've got a ton of work piled up.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.420
Okay.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.090
See you.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:37.960
Bye.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:42.840
Oh, yeah, Kukuru, I'm going 
to be busy for a while, too.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:46.050
The egg Dorayaki-chan laid 
is about to hatch soon.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:48.350
Wow!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:51.180
So I'm going to be working overnight.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.020
That's exciting.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.020
<b>Garandou - Early - Overnight - Off - Late - Overnight - Off - Early</b>

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.020
<b>Haebaru - Early - Early - Early - Early - Off - Early - Early</b>

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.020
<b>Yonekura - Off - Late - Early - Overnight - Off - Overnight - Off</b>

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.020
<b>Miyazawa - Overnight - Off - Overnight - Off - Early - Late - Overnight</b>

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.020
Huh, is it just you and Marina-san 
who are staying overnight?

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.970
What about Haebaru-san?

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:01.470
She said she couldn't make it.

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:02.810
Why not?

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:03.650
Dunno.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.820
Why does she get special treatment?

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:08.600
That's not right.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.920
Let me handle this.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.670
I'll be straight with her.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.620
Wait...

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.620
Don't fight!

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.580
This just isn't right!

00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.210
What isn't?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.380
Are you really all right with pushing 
all that responsibility onto your juniors?

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.240
You're the chief. You're supposed
to be the most responsible.

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.280
I don't know why you can't make it, 
but these shifts aren't fair.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.290
I feel bad for Fuuka and Marina.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.440
Are you done?

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:43.320
I can't believe you don't even want to be there 
when the penguin's about to be born!

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.030
Some people can't be involved with
breeding, even if they want to.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.720
I know that.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:50.840
No, you don't!

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:51.740
You don't know!

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.880
Kukuru-san, we said it's okay, so it's fine.

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:07.140
Thanks, but it's...

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:08.550
Fine.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.820
Shit, I'm going to be late.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:35.220
<b>Churashido Nursery</b>

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:33.130
Thank you for your care.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.200
Yes, see you tomorrow!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.630
Sorry I'm late!

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:50.620
Mama!

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:51.660
Mama!

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:55.020
Thanks for waiting, Shizuku.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:17.950
What's wrong, Shizu-kun?

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.870
Are you not hungry?

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.140
Say, "ah."

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.920
Another fever.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:35.790
Mom?

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.960
Could you take Shizuku 
to the hospital again tomorrow?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.510
Oh, okay.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:44.480
Yeah, it's all right then.

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.060
I'll be fine.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.590
I'll figure it out.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.660
Pardon me.

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:58.160
Kukuru.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:07:59.950
What's up?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.840
Sorry, about the
behind-the-scenes tour today...

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:06.330
Could you handle the penguin commentary?

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:08.430
Sure, but why?

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.920
Haebaru-san called in sick last minute.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.620
Marina-san doesn't have a shift today, either.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.230
That woman talks big all the time,

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:19.680
yet she doesn't take her shifts, 
and she doesn't come to work.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:21.360
She's causing way too much trouble!

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.150
Kukuru-san, it's your chance!

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:24.730
For what?

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.650
If you can do your work as an attendant 
perfectly today in her place,

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:31.870
you might have a chance to get assigned 
as an attendant at the next staff change!

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:32.900
Right!

00:08:33.640 --> 00:08:37.080
Assistant Director, I'd like to go help 
with the penguins,

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.660
since they don't have enough people!

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:39.660
Denied.

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:41.440
Why not?!

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.040
You have your own work.

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:47.660
Then you wouldn't mind if I finish my work first 
and then go help with them, right?

00:08:56.320 --> 00:09:00.930
Sakuramochi and Dorayaki are
taking turns warming up their egg.

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.560
Once it's close to hatching time,

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:07.440
we watch over them through cameras, 
so we can avoid disturbing them.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.850
I heard you took over commentary 
for the penguins.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:12.960
Thanks a lot.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.190
Not at all.

00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:18.070
If it's all right with you, 
I'd like to help with the overnight shift, too.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.610
Well, well...

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:22.670
I appreciate it, 
but I can't ask you to do that.

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:26.690
But Haebaru-san can't make it, can she?

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:29.880
It'll be too hard for Fuuka and
Marina-san to run it by themselves.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:33.210
It sure is great having people's backup.

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:37.070
Haebaru-san's really busy 
with her young child, too.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:42.470
Anyway, I'll go discuss it with the director.

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:47.780
Huh?

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.370
Chiyu, I thought 
you were taking the day off.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.570
I managed to make things work.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.430
So I thought I'd come to work 
from the afternoon.

00:09:56.430 --> 00:09:58.430
You're such a go-getter.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.070
I want to work as much as I can.

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.080
You say that,

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:06.020
but I bet you really just didn't want 
to see Misakino-san do anything to help.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.150
Oh, you didn't know yet?

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:12.840
I heard she's taking your shift temporarily.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:14.340
I'll go ask the boss!

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Garandou - Early - Overnight - Off - Late - Overnight - Off - Early</b>

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Haebaru - Early - Early - Early - Early - Off - Early - Early</b>

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Yonekura - Off - Late - Early - Overnight - Off - Overnight - Off</b>

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Miyazawa - Overnight - Off - Overnight - Off - Early - Late - Overnight</b>

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Misakino -</b>

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.850
Is something wrong, Kukuru?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:30.890
Well...

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.160
What do you think you're doing?!

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.190
Why is your name on here?

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.200
Well...

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:41.950
I never asked you to help 
with attendant work!

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.340
Stick to your own work!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.770
What's going on?

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:45.600
Haebaru-san, please, calm down!

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:46.180
Sounds like they're fighting again.

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.820
Just because you think 
you have some attendant experience...

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:51.020
Could you please not go around 
trampling on other people's turf?

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.240
She just offered to help, 
in case there weren't enough people!

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:54.990
...too.

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:59.880
I want to work, too!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.470
Please don't take my job!

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.980
<b>Shout-Out to The Tattered</b>

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.740
I mean... I understand 
that you want to work hard.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.900
Hey, Haebaru-san...

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:24.400
You're raising your child by yourself.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.780
I'm sure you're going to need the help 
of the people around you.

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.700
Why did you try to hide it?

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:30.750
Because...

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.200
Why don't you go home for today?

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:40.580
You were planning 
to take the day off anyway.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:41.090
Right?

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.340
No, it's fine.

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.100
We can find a replacement.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:49.080
We can't have you 
skipping work all the time!

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.560
The animals are important, 
but you should take care of your child, too.

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:55.860
Okay.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:03.340
Kaoru.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:08.240
Sorry I never told you.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.120
You don't need to apologize.

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.370
But I wish you'd have talked to me.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:15.940
It's not good to deal 
with it all by yourself.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.640
I'll help you out as much as I can.

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:21.910
Thanks.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.470
I had no idea.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:29.160
To think Chiyu-san had a child...

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.470
Seriously?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.430
Yeah. I was shocked.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.140
Wow, that's badass!

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.480
She has a child, 
and she's working her ass off.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.460
I feel torn.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.950
How so?

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:43.070
I said a lot of terrible things to her.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.110
She couldn't blame you for that.

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:49.630
Besides, I thought it'd be all right 
that I took her shift.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:51.580
I didn't think she'd react like that.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.000
React how?

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:54.900
She was angry.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:57.450
And frustrated with herself.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:12:59.740
And about to cry.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.280
She was actually crying.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.480
That's kind of sad.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.520
<b>Misakino Kukuru</b>

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:14.820
<i>Hello? Kukuru?</i>

00:13:15.520 --> 00:13:16.660
Fuuka?

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:18.120
<i>Yeah?</i>

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:23.320
I've never liked Haebaru-san up to now.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:27.050
I still don't like her.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:30.350
But when I think that maybe
she's been fighting on her own

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.040
because she loves aquarium work...

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.040
<i>I can't help but relate.</i>

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.090
Yeah.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:43.480
I want to get to know
Haebaru-san a bit better.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:45.050
<i>Me, too.</i>

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.820
So I was thinking...

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:51.910
Why don't I try experiencing 
the same burdens that she has?

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:53.270
<i>"The same"?</i>

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.640
I'm going to try raising a kid.

00:13:58.320 --> 00:13:59.720
Morning!

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:00.770
Come in!

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.740
Thanks so much for taking a half day 
to look after my child.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:07.880
Not at all.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.700
Sorry for making such a demand.

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:14.580
I can finally go to the hairdresser
now, though. Thanks!

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:17.120
I don't even know how many months it's been.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.580
Really?

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:22.590
You just don't have any free time 
when you have a kid.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:24.940
Here are his diapers and milk.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.840
I wrote down all the small things.

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.690
I should be back in about two hours.

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.220
Huh? That's it?

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.760
Bye!

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:34.920
No way.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:47.080
He's so tiny and cute!

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:56.160
No way!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.330
There, there.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:14:59.920
Mommy's here!

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.260
Miyazawa-san?

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.840
How's your child doing?

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:18.520
Okay now, I think.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.860
Thank goodness.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:23.040
So, what brings you here?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.150
I wanted to hear about you.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:28.530
I want to get to know you better.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:31.530
I don't want to talk.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.360
You don't have to tell me everything.

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:38.850
But isn't it normal to want 
to get to know your coworkers,

00:15:38.850 --> 00:15:42.920
so you can help each other out more?

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.420
Is that how Gama Gama did things?

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.650
I'm being serious!

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:51.720
Kuuya-san's helping out 
with the penguins today.

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:54.440
You may not like it,

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:58.220
but work is happening with the help 
of the people from Gama Gama.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.720
I graduated when I was eighteen

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.510
and became an attendant, 
which I've always wanted to do.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:22.220
Soon after I started work, 
I got married and had my child.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:27.220
I was still young, and I still had trouble 
working at the same time.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.750
<b>Haebaru Chiyu - Off</b>

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:33.290
The people at work were cooperative at first, 
but eventually they grew colder.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:39.320
In the end, I got fired, 
and my family fell apart.

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:42.890
I got divorced and came
back home to Okinawa.

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:47.900
<b>Staff wanted for large-scale 
aquarium opening in March, 2022!</b>

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:47.900
Right when I was getting used to being a parent, 
I learned about Tingarla opening.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:52.440
I studied like crazy 
and managed to get hired.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.910
And I decided to hide the fact 
that I have a child.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:02.330
I wasn't going to lose
my dream job this time.

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.540
I'm glad you told me.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:16.300
I think I understand a little better 
why you didn't like the Gama Gama crew.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.580
That's right.

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.820
I hate Misakino-san.

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:22.810
She takes working 
at an aquarium for granted.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:27.530
And she takes everyone 
helping her out for granted.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.890
But just the same, 
Kukuru thinks it's obvious

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:35.070
that she has to help 
the people around her, too.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:41.440
She's experiencing parenting 
right about now,

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:43.580
to try to understand 
what you go through.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:44.450
What?

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.310
Thank you for the coffee.

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.030
I should get going now.

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:55.430
I'm looking forward 
to your return to work, Chief.

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:05.940
I'm back!

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.760
Is everything all right?

00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:12.500
He was crying the whole time.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:14.690
I tried holding him and everything, 
but nothing worked.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.700
I'm sorry! It must have been difficult.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.280
There, there, Haru-kun.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.750
Mommy's here.

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:24.410
It's so rough. I'm amazed 
you work on top of all this.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:26.170
You mean me?

00:18:26.170 --> 00:18:27.160
Or Haebaru-san?

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.920
Both of you!

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:34.190
I guess this hands-on training 
was useful, then?

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.800
Yes. Very.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:40.470
Gramps said to everyone 
when Gama Gama closed...

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:44.400
That he wants us all 
to love living things,

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:49.480
and that he wants people working 
at aquariums to be kinder than anyone.

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.300
People are living things, too.

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:56.880
I want to become kinder.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:01.260
To the fish and to the
people around me, too.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.380
This is my son, Shizuku.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.750
Hello.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.500
I'm sorry for hiding the fact 
that I had a child.

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.790
I'm going to be causing trouble.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:23.760
What?! He's adorable!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:26.080
Why did you hide him from us?

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:27.520
No fair!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:31.640
Chiyu-san, why don't you show
Shizuku-kun around the facility?

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.980
I don't want to cause trouble.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.400
Don't worry about it!

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.880
I'll go ask the director 
for permission!

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:40.900
No...

00:19:41.810 --> 00:19:45.080
You want to see Mom working, don't you?

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:45.910
Yeah!

00:19:57.600 --> 00:19:59.530
Mommy, what's this?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.940
Rainbow mantis shrimp.

00:20:03.570 --> 00:20:04.930
Mommy, what's this?

00:20:10.820 --> 00:20:12.640
I'm sorry, Director.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.160
Not at all.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:17.400
Show him everything.

00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:25.180
Shizuku-kun, your mommy 
is <i>really</i> important to Tingarla.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.910
She's the animals' mommy, too.

00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:30.410
You're awesome, Mommy!

00:20:33.320 --> 00:20:35.860
Thanks, Shizu-kun.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.090
Mommy, look! Look!

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.600
All these fish!

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:03.400
I'm sorry about the shift.

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:07.070
No, I didn't realize, either.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:13.480
Haebaru-san, are you an aquarium freak?

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.670
I am, too.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:19.670
I know that.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:26.730
Let's both work our asses off 
for the creatures we love!

00:21:28.840 --> 00:21:33.020
Damn it. You Gama Gama people are so stuffy.

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:39.520
It's started pecking!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.250
Yay!
